ange)</td><td align="center">0.95 (0.78&#x02013;1.20)</td><td align="center">0.94 (0.77&#x02013;1.16)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Diastolic dysfunction, n(%)</td><td align="center">97 (24.1)</td><td align="center">74 (29.0)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Stage C of heart failure (symptomatic cardiac dysfunction), n(%)</td><td align="center">35 (8.4)</td><td align="center">14 (5.2)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>*Valid values available for 541 participants.</p><p>CHD, coronary heart disease; FHS, Framingham Heart Study; LVSD, left ventricular systolic dysfunction; LV, left ventricle; FFM, fat-free mass</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Cardiac structure and function parameters according to number of features of metabolic syndrome, adjusted for age and gender.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td align="center" colspan="5">Number of features of the metabolic syndrome</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan="5"><hr></hr></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">4&#x02013;5</td><td align="center">p (trend)</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center">n = 94</td><td align="center">n = 229</td><td align="center">n = 226</td><td align="center">n = 79</td><td align="center">n = 56</td><td></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left"><bold>Adjusted prevalence (95%CI)</bold></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Stage C of heart failure</td><td align="center">2.4 (0.6&#x02013;9.2)</td><td align="center">4.0 (2.2&#x02013;7.3)</td><td align="center">4.7 (2.7&#x02013;8.3)</td><td align="center">8.1 (4.0&#x02013;15.7)</td><td align="center">10.5 (5.1&#x02013;20.5)</td><td align="center">0.007</td></tr><tr><td align="left">LVSD</td><td align="center">0.0 (0.0-0.0)</td><